w I want to say something here that is  sort of maybe surprising to some which  is that I don't know that this is bad in  every sense and I'm gonna try to explain  what I mean right one interpretation of  what Merkel is saying is you know Europe  can't count on the United States  military it's an indictment of Trump's  foreign policy it's an indictment of  diplomacy under Trump and  and there's this idea which is I think  an accurate one that the u.s. is an  increasingly erratic player even though  our European alliances go back a long  time and we're considered to be serious  and lasting European allies can't really  trust anymore that the United States is  going to be there in shared defense of  Europe whatever may come up that's true  that's a concern and it's something I've  been talking about a lot which is if the  US can't be counted on to stick the  deals and stick with allies our  diplomatic power is very much hurt  because other countries can't trust us  and in fact that plays directly into the  Russian strategy which is hey let's  cause as much chaos as possible in the  diplomatic West interfering in  partnerships between the United States  and allies is something that is a huge  win for the Russian geopolitical  strategic goals breaking the Iran deal  is part of it putting cracks in our  relationships with our allies as part of  it and this is why Russia would prefer  Trump over Hillary but I want to mention  another side to this which is that in a  sense isn't it good in a way for the  expectation of the US as the world's  policeman to go away right this is not  me being an isolationist but we  shouldn't want the world to expect that  the United States will come to the  rescue  at any time and I want to be clear if we  have an alliance if we've made a deal if  we're part of NATO if we're part of the  Iran deal we should stick to the deal we  should hold up our end of the bargain  I'm not cheering bailing on deals but  from the point of view of resisting 